# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste your TypeSafe API key after the `=`.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Get a key at https://typesafe.ai. Leave it empty (or skip .env.local entirely)
# to run in demo mode: routing decisions are simulated with keyword matching and
# the UI is clearly labeled "Demo mode — simulated, not real Jev calls."
#
# The key is only ever read on the server (app/api/route/route.ts). It is never
# sent to the browser. Do NOT prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Jev model id (defaults to jev-latest).
# JEV_MODEL=jev-latest

# Optional: how many routing calls per minute may be made with the SERVER key
# above. Calls that carry a browser-saved key are not counted: they spend that
# user's credits, not yours. Default 60; 0 disables the limit. The counter is
# per process, so treat it as a brake, not a hard quota.
# ROUTE_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=60

# Optional: set to 1 when a proxy you control (Vercel, nginx, a load balancer)
# sits in front of the app and overwrites x-forwarded-for / x-real-ip with the
# real client address. The limit above is then applied per client IP. Leave it
# unset otherwise: those headers are client-controlled when the app is reached
# directly, so they are ignored and all callers share one bucket.
# ROUTE_TRUST_PROXY=1
